      "id": 12879,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-16T22:15:58.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ra, Expatriette, and Visionary vs. The Matriarch in Insula Primalis. How to win? That order of characters, as I rather think it would be easier if you put Visionary first.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've suffered four massive defeats in a row. I've tried just focusing fire on The Matriarch. I tried using Twist The Ether and Liquid Nitrogen Rounds to reduce The Matriarch's attacks, but amongst Horrid Cacophany, Huginn, and Primordial Plant Life, couldn't keep them in play. Same thing with Flame Barrier.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I had a great start once, with two useless Darken The Skies and a mostly painless Horrid Cacophany followed by Brain Burning The Mask. It wasn't enough. The Matriarch flipped and started healing when she was only down to the 40s for hit points, but the heroes were already in the low teens.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I tried carefully dealing with each threat as it came out, but of course that just meant that I did a ton of damage to Cohorts and Carrion Fields rather than The Matriarch.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:32.197Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
